# Android (TWA) — see android/README.md
# The signing key and its password are the app's identity: anything signed with
# this key is trusted as an update to the installed app, and anything signed
# with a different key CANNOT update it (Android refuses; the app has to be
# uninstalled and reinstalled first). So it must never be committed, and it must
# never be lost. Back both files up somewhere private and off this machine.
android/*.keystore
android/keystore-password.txt
# Bubblewrap's generated Android project — regenerated by `npm run android:build`
# from `android/twa-manifest.json`, which IS committed. Build output and the
# Gradle wrapper it downloads have no business in git.
android/app/
android/build/
android/.gradle/
android/gradle/
android/gradlew
android/gradlew.bat
android/gradle.properties
android/settings.gradle
android/build.gradle
android/store_icon.png
android/*.apk
android/*.aab
android/*.idsig
